module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Descent.PullbackDescentData
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Pullback.ChosenPullback
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Effective descent along a family from effective descent along a refinement

Let `𝒰 = {U i ⟶ U}` and `𝒱 = {V j ⟶ U}` be families of morphisms with fixed target in a
category `C`, and let `Φ : 𝒱 ⟶ 𝒰` be a morphism of such families over `𝟙 U`, that is a
reindexing `α : J ⟶ I` together with morphisms `V j ⟶ U (α j)` over `U`, so that `𝒱` refines
`𝒰`. Let `p : 𝒳 ⥤ C` be a fibred category, write `𝒮_U` for its fibre over `U` and `DD(𝒰)` for
the category `CategoryTheory.Functor.FamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰` of descent data relative to `𝒰`.

This file proves Stacks 0GEA: if the fibre products `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`, `U i ×_U V j` and
`U i₁ ×_U U i₂ ×_U V j` exist, if `𝒮_U ⟶ DD(𝒱)` is an equivalence, if `𝒮_{U i} ⟶ DD(𝒱_i)` is
fully faithful for every `i`, and if `𝒮_{U i₁ ×_U U i₂} ⟶ DD(𝒱_{i₁i₂})` is faithful for every
`i₁, i₂`, then `𝒮_U ⟶ DD(𝒰)` is an equivalence. Here `𝒱_i = {U i ×_U V j ⟶ U i}` and
`𝒱_{i₁i₂} = {U i₁ ×_U U i₂ ×_U V j ⟶ U i₁ ×_U U i₂}` are the base changes of `𝒱`.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.toFamilyDescentDatum`, the functor `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒰)` sending an object of
  the fibre over `U` to its canonical descent datum;
* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.refSieve`, the sieve on `Over.mk a` corresponding to
  the pullback along `q` of the sieve generated by a family;
* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.glue`, the morphism between the components of two
  descent data obtained by gluing a morphism between their refinements;
* `CategoryTheory.Limits.ChosenPullback.ofHasPullback`, the chosen pullback given by
  `CategoryTheory.Limits.pullback`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.Functor.isEquivalence_toFamilyDescentDatum_of_homOver`, Stacks 0GEA;
* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.bijective_pullFunctor_map`, descent of morphisms
  between two fixed descent data along the refinement, from hypotheses at their components only;
* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor`, full
  faithfulness of the refinement functor `DD(𝒰) ⥤ DD(𝒱)` of Stacks 02ZD under local hypotheses;
* `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.comm_of_chosenPullback`, the reduction of the
  compatibility of a family of morphisms with the gluing isomorphisms of two descent data to the
  chosen fibre products;
* `CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover.ofArrows_pullback₁`, the sieve generated by a base changed
  family is the pullback of the sieve generated by the family.

## Implementation notes

The proof runs through full faithfulness of the refinement functor `DD(𝒰) ⥤ DD(𝒱)` of
Stacks 02ZD (`CategoryTheory.Functor.FamilyDescentDatum.pullFunctor`). Composing `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒰)`
with it gives a functor isomorphic to `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒱)`, which is an equivalence by hypothesis (2);
full faithfulness of the refinement functor then transfers full faithfulness and essential
surjectivity back to `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒰)`. The source instead constructs the essential surjectivity by
hand from hypothesis (3) and omits the full faithfulness of `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒰)` altogether; both
omitted verifications are supplied by this route, and hypotheses (2), (3) and (4) are used
exactly where the source uses them.

Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.fullyFaithfulPullFunctor` also proves full
faithfulness of a refinement functor, but from a *global* `[F.IsPrestack J]` together with the
hypothesis that the refining family is `J`-covering. Hypotheses (3) and (4) of 0GEA are *local*,
being conditions at the single objects `U i` and `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`, and neither hypothesis set
implies the other, so Mathlib's statement cannot be used. The argument is therefore redone here
from precisely the two conditions that proof consumes: the sheaf condition for the presheaf of
morphisms along the pullback of the sieve generated by `𝒱` to each `U i`, and its separatedness
along the pullback to each chosen fibre product `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`. That local form is
`nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor`.

Both of those conditions are asked only **at the components of the two descent data between
which morphisms are being descended**, and not at arbitrary objects `M N` of the fibres, because
that is all the proof uses: the amalgamation in `glue` is of a family of elements of
`F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i)`, and the separatedness in `comm_glue` and in the
injectivity argument is of the same presheaf. The per-pair statement is
`bijective_pullFunctor_map`, and `nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor` is its quantification over
all pairs. This matters because the fpqc sheaf condition for the presheaf of morphisms of
`𝒪`-modules is available for *quasi-coherent* modules only, so the form quantified over all `M N`
— equivalently `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack` — is not available for fpqc while the
per-pair form at quasi-coherent components is.

Descent data are Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData` for the pullback
pseudofunctor of `p` (Stacks 02XO), so their gluing morphisms are indexed by an arbitrary object
mapping to two members of the family rather than by a fibre product of two members. Hypothesis
(1) of the source is consequently not needed to give the categories `DD(𝒰)` and `DD(𝒱)` a
meaning; it is needed only to form the base changed families `𝒱_i` and `𝒱_{i₁i₂}`, which is why
only the sub-list `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`, `U i ×_U V j` and `U i₁ ×_U U i₂ ×_U V j` of the source's
fibre products — the cases `(p, q) = (2, 0), (1, 1), (2, 1)` of its enumeration — is assumed
here. That is a *weaker* hypothesis than the source's (1), so the result proved is slightly more
general than 0GEA. In particular `HasPullbacks C` is deliberately **not** assumed: it would be
stronger than hypothesis (1) and would make the statement a weakening of the source's.

Because the gluing morphisms are indexed by arbitrary objects, the compatibility a morphism of
descent data must satisfy is a condition over every object mapping to two members of `𝒰`, and
not merely over the fibre products. `comm_of_chosenPullback` shows that the condition over the
chosen fibre products implies the condition over every object, by pulling the square back along
the induced morphism. This is what makes hypothesis (4), a condition at `U i₁ ×_U U i₂` only,
enough.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GEA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GEA)
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option backward.defeqAttrib.useBackward true
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

universe w' w t t' v' v₂ v u' u₂ u

namespace CategoryTheory

open Opposite Limits Pseudofunctor Pseudofunctor.LocallyDiscreteOpToCat

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C]

namespace Pseudofunctor.DescentData

variable {F : Pseudofunctor (LocallyDiscrete Cᵒᵖ) Cat.{v', u'}}
  {ι : Type t} {S : C} {X : ι → C} {f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ S}

/-- The compatibility of a family of morphisms `hom i : D₁.obj i ⟶ D₂.obj i` with the gluing
isomorphisms of two descent data over an arbitrary object `Y` mapping to two members of the
family follows from the compatibility over chosen fibre products. -/
lemma comm_of_chosenPullback {D₁ D₂ : F.DescentData f}
    (sq : ∀ i₁ i₂, ChosenPullback (f i₁) (f i₂))
    (hom : ∀ i, D₁.obj i ⟶ D₂.obj i)
    (comm : ∀ i₁ i₂,
      (F.map (sq i₁ i₂).p₁.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (hom i₁) ≫
          D₂.hom (sq i₁ i₂).p (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p₂ =
        D₁.hom (sq i₁ i₂).p (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p₂ ≫
          (F.map (sq i₁ i₂).p₂.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (hom i₂))
    ⦃Y : C⦄ (q : Y ⟶ S) ⦃i₁ i₂ : ι⦄ (a₁ : Y ⟶ X i₁) (a₂ : Y ⟶ X i₂)
    (ha₁ : a₁ ≫ f i₁ = q := by cat_disch) (ha₂ : a₂ ≫ f i₂ = q := by cat_disch) :
    (F.map a₁.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (hom i₁) ≫ D₂.hom q a₁ a₂ ha₁ ha₂ =
      D₁.hom q a₁ a₂ ha₁ ha₂ ≫ (F.map a₂.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (hom i₂) := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr₁, hr₂⟩ := (sq i₁ i₂).isPullback.exists_lift a₁ a₂ (by rw [ha₁, ha₂])
  have hq : r ≫ (sq i₁ i₂).p = q := by
    rw [← (sq i₁ i₂).hp₁, reassoc_of% hr₁, ha₁]
  rw [← D₂.pullHom_hom r (sq i₁ i₂).p q hq (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p₂
        (sq i₁ i₂).hp₁ (sq i₁ i₂).hp₂ a₁ a₂ hr₁ hr₂,
    ← D₁.pullHom_hom r (sq i₁ i₂).p q hq (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p₂
        (sq i₁ i₂).hp₁ (sq i₁ i₂).hp₂ a₁ a₂ hr₁ hr₂]
  dsimp only [pullHom]
  rw [NatTrans.naturality_assoc]
  dsimp
  rw [← Functor.map_comp_assoc, comm i₁ i₂, Functor.map_comp_assoc, mapComp'_inv_naturality]
  simp [Category.assoc]

section Refinement

variable {ι' : Type t'} {X' : ι' → C} {f' : ∀ j, X' j ⟶ S}
  {α : ι' → ι} {p' : ∀ j, X' j ⟶ X (α j)} (w : ∀ j, p' j ≫ f (α j) = f' j)

include w in
/-- The compatibility `w` of a refinement, in the form the pullback functor on descent data asks
for when the morphism of targets is `𝟙 S`.

This is given a name rather than left to `cat_disch` inside the statements below because a
tactic block in the type of a declaration elaborates to a module-private auxiliary constant,
which makes the declaration unusable from any other module. -/
lemma w_comp_id (j : ι') : p' j ≫ f (α j) = f' j ≫ 𝟙 S := by
  rw [Category.comp_id]
  exact w j

variable (f f') in
/-- Given two families of morphisms `f i : X i ⟶ S` and `f' j : X' j ⟶ S` and a morphism
`a : W ⟶ T` with `q : W ⟶ S`, this is the sieve on `Over.mk a : Over T` which corresponds to
the sieve on `W` obtained by pulling back along `q` the sieve generated by `f'`. -/
abbrev refSieve {T W : C} (a : W ⟶ T) (q : W ⟶ S) : Sieve (Over.mk a) :=
  (Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk a)).symm (Sieve.pullback q (Sieve.ofArrows X' f'))

/-- A morphism `r : Z ⟶ X i` lies in `refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i)` as soon as `r ≫ f i` factors
through some `f' j`. -/
lemma mem_refSieve {i : ι} {Z : C} (r : Z ⟶ X i) ⦃j : ι'⦄ (b : Z ⟶ X' j)
    (fac : b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i := by cat_disch) :
    refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i) (Over.homMk r : Over.mk r ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 (X i))) :=
  ⟨_, b, f' j, ⟨j⟩, fac⟩

/-- Any morphism `g : Z ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 X)` in `Over X` is `Over.homMk Z.hom`. -/
private lemma eq_homMk_hom {X : C} {Z : Over X} (g : Z ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 X)) :
    g = Over.homMk Z.hom := by
  ext
  simpa using Over.w g

namespace refSieve

variable {i : ι} {Z : C} {r : Z ⟶ X i}
  (hr : refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i) (Over.homMk r : Over.mk r ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 (X i))))

include hr in
/-- If `r` lies in `refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i)`, then `r ≫ f i` factors through some `f' j`. -/
lemma exists_fac : ∃ (j : ι') (b : Z ⟶ X' j), b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i := by
  obtain ⟨_, b, _, ⟨j⟩, fac⟩ := hr
  exact ⟨j, b, fac⟩

/-- A choice of index `j` for which `r` factors through `f' j` after composing with `f i`. -/
noncomputable def idx : ι' := (exists_fac hr).choose

/-- A choice of factorization of `r ≫ f i` through `f' (idx hr)`. -/
noncomputable def hom : Z ⟶ X' (idx hr) := (exists_fac hr).choose_spec.choose

/-- The factorization `hom hr ≫ f' (idx hr) = r ≫ f i`. -/
@[reassoc]
lemma fac : hom hr ≫ f' (idx hr) = r ≫ f i := (exists_fac hr).choose_spec.choose_spec

end refSieve

section Pair

variable {D₁ D₂ : F.DescentData f}
  (φ : (pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p') (w_comp_id w)).obj D₁ ⟶
    (pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p') (w_comp_id w)).obj D₂)

/-- Given a morphism `φ` between the images of `D₁` and `D₂` under a refinement functor, and a
factorization `b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i`, this is the section of the presheaf of morphisms from
`D₁.obj i` to `D₂.obj i` over `Over.mk r` obtained by pulling back `φ.hom j`. -/
def mor ⦃i : ι⦄ {Z : C} (r : Z ⟶ X i) ⦃j : ι'⦄ (b : Z ⟶ X' j)
    (fac : b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i := by cat_disch) :
    (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i)).obj (op (Over.mk r)) :=
  D₁.hom (r ≫ f i) r (b ≫ p' j) ≫ pullHom (φ.hom j) b _ _ ≫ D₂.hom (r ≫ f i) (b ≫ p' j) r

/-- The expression of `mor w φ r b fac` with the morphisms `r ≫ f i` and `b ≫ p' j` replaced by
equal morphisms `q'` and `b'`. -/
lemma mor_eq ⦃i : ι⦄ {Z : C} (r : Z ⟶ X i) ⦃j : ι'⦄ (b : Z ⟶ X' j)
    (fac : b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i) (q' : Z ⟶ S) (b' : Z ⟶ X (α j))
    (hq' : r ≫ f i = q' := by cat_disch) (hb' : b ≫ p' j = b' := by cat_disch) :
    mor w φ r b fac =
      D₁.hom q' r b' ≫ pullHom (φ.hom j) b _ _ ≫ D₂.hom q' b' r := by
  subst hq' hb'
  rfl

include w φ in
/-- The section `mor w φ` is compatible with precomposition: its value at `s ≫ r` is the
restriction along `Over.homMk s` of its value at `r`. -/
lemma mor_precomp ⦃i : ι⦄ {Z : C} (r : Z ⟶ X i) ⦃j : ι'⦄ (b : Z ⟶ X' j)
    (fac : b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i) {Z' : C} (s : Z' ⟶ Z)
    (r' : Z' ⟶ X i) (b' : Z' ⟶ X' j) (hr' : s ≫ r = r' := by cat_disch)
    (hb' : s ≫ b = b' := by cat_disch) :
    mor w φ r' b' (by cat_disch) =
      (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i)).map (Over.homMk s).op (mor w φ r b fac) := by
  dsimp
  rw [mor_eq _ _ _ _ _ (s ≫ r ≫ f i) (s ≫ b ≫ p' j),
    mor_eq _ _ _ _ _ _ _ rfl rfl,
    ← D₁.pullHom_hom s (r ≫ f i) _ rfl r (b ≫ p' j) rfl (by cat_disch) r' _ hr' rfl,
    ← D₂.pullHom_hom s (r ≫ f i) _ rfl (b ≫ p' j) r (by cat_disch) rfl _ r' rfl hr']
  have := F.mapComp'_naturality_2 b.op.toLoc s.op.toLoc b'.op.toLoc (by cat_disch) (φ.hom j)
  dsimp [pullHom] at this ⊢
  simp only [Category.assoc, Functor.map_comp, ← this,
    Cat.Hom.inv_hom_id_toNatTrans_app_assoc,
    mapComp'₀₁₃_hom_comp_whiskerLeft_mapComp'_hom_app_assoc F
    (p' j).op.toLoc b.op.toLoc s.op.toLoc ((p' j).op.toLoc ≫ b.op.toLoc) b'.op.toLoc
      (((p' j).op.toLoc ≫ b.op.toLoc) ≫ s.op.toLoc) rfl (by grind) (by grind),
    ← mapComp'_inv_whiskerRight_mapComp'₀₂₃_inv_app_assoc F
    (p' j).op.toLoc b.op.toLoc s.op.toLoc ((p' j).op.toLoc ≫ b.op.toLoc) b'.op.toLoc
      (((p' j).op.toLoc ≫ b.op.toLoc) ≫ s.op.toLoc) rfl (by grind) (by grind)]

/-- The section `mor w φ r b fac` does not depend on the choice of the factorization of `r ≫ f i`
through the family `f'`. -/
lemma mor_unique ⦃i : ι⦄ {Z : C} (r : Z ⟶ X i)
    ⦃j₁ : ι'⦄ (b₁ : Z ⟶ X' j₁) ⦃j₂ : ι'⦄ (b₂ : Z ⟶ X' j₂)
    (fac₁ : b₁ ≫ f' j₁ = r ≫ f i := by cat_disch)
    (fac₂ : b₂ ≫ f' j₂ = r ≫ f i := by cat_disch) :
    mor w φ r b₁ fac₁ = mor w φ r b₂ fac₂ := by
  have := φ.comm (r ≫ f i) b₁ b₂ fac₁ fac₂
  dsimp at this
  rw [pullFunctorObjHom_eq _ _ _ _ _ (r ≫ f i) (b₁ ≫ p' j₁) (b₂ ≫ p' j₂) rfl,
    pullFunctorObjHom_eq _ _ _ _ _ (r ≫ f i) (b₁ ≫ p' j₁) (b₂ ≫ p' j₂) rfl,
    map_eq_pullHom _ _ _ _ (by exact rfl) rfl, map_eq_pullHom _ _ _ _ rfl rfl] at this
  dsimp at this
  simp only [Category.assoc, Cat.Hom.hom_inv_id_toNatTrans_app_assoc, cancel_epi] at this
  simp only [← Category.assoc, cancel_mono] at this
  rw [← cancel_mono (D₂.hom (r ≫ f i) (b₂ ≫ p' j₂) r), Category.assoc,
    D₂.hom_comp] at this
  rw [mor_eq _ _ _ _ _ _ _ rfl rfl, mor_eq _ _ _ _ _ _ _ rfl rfl, this]
  simp

/-- The family of elements of the presheaf of morphisms from `D₁.obj i` to `D₂.obj i`, over the
sieve on `Over.mk (𝟙 (X i))` obtained by pulling back the sieve generated by `f'`, deduced
from `φ`. -/
noncomputable def familyOfElements (i : ι) :
    Presieve.FamilyOfElements (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i))
      (refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i)).arrows :=
  fun Z r hr ↦
    mor w φ _ _ (refSieve.fac (f := f) (f' := f') (r := Z.hom) (by
      convert! hr
      ext
      simpa using (Over.w r).symm))

/-- The value of `familyOfElements w φ i` at `g : Z ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 (X i))` is `mor w φ Z.hom b fac`
for any factorization `b ≫ f' j = Z.hom ≫ f i`. -/
lemma familyOfElements_eq {i : ι} {Z : Over (X i)} (g : Z ⟶ Over.mk (𝟙 (X i)))
    ⦃j : ι'⦄ (b : Z.left ⟶ X' j) (fac : b ≫ f' j = Z.hom ≫ f i := by cat_disch) :
    familyOfElements w φ i g (by
      rw [show g = Over.homMk Z.hom by ext; simpa using Over.w g]
      exact mem_refSieve _ b fac) = mor w φ _ b fac :=
  mor_unique _ _ _ _ _ _ _

/-- The family of elements `familyOfElements w φ i` is compatible. -/
lemma compatible_familyOfElements (i : ι) :
    (familyOfElements w φ i).Compatible := by
  intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ h₁ h₂ hh₁ hh₂ fac
  obtain rfl := eq_homMk_hom h₁
  obtain rfl := eq_homMk_hom h₂
  obtain ⟨g₁, hg₁, rfl⟩ := Over.homMk_surjective g₁
  obtain ⟨g₂, hg₂, rfl⟩ := Over.homMk_surjective g₂
  obtain ⟨_, b₁, _, ⟨j₁⟩, fac₁⟩ := hh₁
  obtain ⟨_, b₂, _, ⟨j₂⟩, fac₂⟩ := hh₂
  dsimp at *
  rw [familyOfElements_eq _ _ _ _ (by simpa using fac₁),
    familyOfElements_eq _ _ _ _ (by simpa using fac₂),
    ← dsimp% mor_precomp w φ Y₁.hom b₁ (by simpa using fac₁) _ _ _ hg₁ rfl,
    ← dsimp% mor_precomp w φ Y₂.hom b₂ (by simpa using fac₂) _ _ _ hg₂ rfl]
  apply mor_unique

variable (H₃ : ∀ i : ι, Presieve.IsSheafFor (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i))
  (refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i)).arrows)

/-- The morphism `D₁.obj i ⟶ D₂.obj i` obtained from `φ` by gluing, using the descent of
morphisms along the pullback of the sieve generated by `f'` to `X i`. -/
noncomputable def glue (i : ι) : D₁.obj i ⟶ D₂.obj i :=
  F.presheafHomObjHomEquiv.symm
    (Presieve.IsSheafFor.amalgamate (H₃ i) _ (compatible_familyOfElements w φ i))

/-- The pullback of `glue w φ H₃ i` along `r : Y ⟶ X i` is `mor w φ r b fac`, for any
factorization `b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i`. -/
lemma map_glue ⦃i : ι⦄ ⦃Y : C⦄ (r : Y ⟶ X i) ⦃j : ι'⦄
    (b : Y ⟶ X' j) (fac : b ≫ f' j = r ≫ f i := by cat_disch) :
    (F.map r.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (glue w φ H₃ i) = mor w φ r b fac := by
  have hs : (familyOfElements w φ i).IsAmalgamation
      (Presieve.IsSheafFor.amalgamate (H₃ i) _ (compatible_familyOfElements w φ i)) :=
    Presieve.IsSheafFor.isAmalgamation (H₃ i) (compatible_familyOfElements w φ i)
  simpa [glue, familyOfElements_eq w φ (Z := Over.mk r) _ b fac,
    presheafHomObjHomEquiv, pullHom, mapComp'_id_comp_hom_app,
    mapComp'_id_comp_inv_app] using hs _ (mem_refSieve _ b fac)

/-- The glued morphisms are compatible with the gluing isomorphisms of `D₁` and `D₂` over any
object `W` for which the descent of morphisms along the pullback of the sieve generated by
`f'` to `W` is separated. -/
lemma comm_glue ⦃W : C⦄ (q : W ⟶ S) ⦃i₁ i₂ : ι⦄
    (a₁ : W ⟶ X i₁) (a₂ : W ⟶ X i₂) (ha₁ : a₁ ≫ f i₁ = q := by cat_disch)
    (ha₂ : a₂ ≫ f i₂ = q := by cat_disch)
    (H : Presieve.IsSeparatedFor (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i₁) (D₂.obj i₁))
      (refSieve f' a₁ q).arrows) :
    (F.map a₁.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (glue w φ H₃ i₁) ≫ D₂.hom q a₁ a₂ =
    D₁.hom q a₁ a₂ ≫ (F.map a₂.op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (glue w φ H₃ i₂) := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (D₂.hom q a₂ a₁), Category.assoc,
    Category.assoc, DescentData.hom_comp, D₂.hom_self _ _ ha₁, Category.comp_id]
  refine H.ext ?_
  rintro T p ⟨_, g, _, ⟨j⟩, fac⟩
  obtain ⟨T, t, rfl⟩ := T.mk_surjective
  obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := Over.homMk_surjective p
  dsimp [pullHom] at t g p hp fac ⊢
  subst hp
  simp only [mapComp'_inv_naturality, Cat.Hom.comp_toFunctor, Functor.comp_obj,
    Cat.Hom.hom_inv_id_toNatTrans_app_assoc, Functor.map_comp, Category.assoc]
  rw [← F.mapComp'_naturality_1 a₂.op.toLoc p.op.toLoc (p ≫ a₂).op.toLoc (by grind),
    map_glue _ _ _ _ g (by grind), map_glue _ _ _ _ g (by grind),
    mor_eq _ _ _ _ (by grind) (p ≫ q) _ (by grind) rfl,
    mor_eq _ _ _ _ (by grind) (p ≫ q) _ (by grind) rfl,
    map_eq_pullHom _ _ _ _ rfl rfl, map_eq_pullHom _ _ _ _ rfl rfl,
    pullHom_hom _ _ _ _ rfl _ _ ha₁ ha₂ _ _ rfl rfl,
    pullHom_hom _ _ _ _ rfl _ _ ha₂ ha₁ _ _ rfl rfl]
  simp

variable (sq : ∀ i₁ i₂, ChosenPullback (f i₁) (f i₂))
  (H₄ : ∀ i₁ i₂ : ι, Presieve.IsSeparatedFor (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i₁) (D₂.obj i₁))
    (refSieve f' (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p).arrows)

include w H₃ H₄ in
/-- **The refinement functor is surjective on morphisms out of `D₁` into `D₂`.**
Every morphism between the restrictions of `D₁` and `D₂` is the restriction of a morphism
`D₁ ⟶ D₂`, obtained by gluing its components with `glue`. Only the descent of morphisms
between the components of `D₁` and `D₂` is used. -/
lemma surjective_pullFunctor_map :
    Function.Surjective ((pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p')
      (w_comp_id w)).map : (D₁ ⟶ D₂) → _) := by
  intro φ
  refine ⟨{ hom := glue w φ H₃
            comm := comm_of_chosenPullback sq _ (fun i₁ i₂ ↦
              comm_glue w φ H₃ _ _ _ (sq i₁ i₂).hp₁ (sq i₁ i₂).hp₂ (H₄ i₁ i₂)) }, ?_⟩
  ext i
  dsimp
  rw [map_glue _ _ _ _ (𝟙 _) (by cat_disch),
    mor_eq _ _ _ _ _ (f' i) (p' i), pullHom_id,
    D₁.hom_self _ _ (by cat_disch), D₂.hom_self _ _ (by cat_disch),
    Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id]

include w H₃ in
/-- **The refinement functor is injective on morphisms out of `D₁` into `D₂`.**
Two morphisms `D₁ ⟶ D₂` with the same restriction are equal. Only the separatedness half of
the descent of morphisms between the components of `D₁` and `D₂` is used. -/
lemma injective_pullFunctor_map :
    Function.Injective ((pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p')
      (w_comp_id w)).map : (D₁ ⟶ D₂) → _) := by
  intro φ φ' hφ
  ext i
  refine F.presheafHomObjHomEquiv.injective ?_
  refine (H₃ i).isSeparatedFor.ext ?_
  rintro Z g ⟨Y, b, c, ⟨j⟩, hb⟩
  obtain rfl := eq_homMk_hom g
  dsimp at b hb
  have (ψ : D₁ ⟶ D₂) :
    (F.presheafHom _ _).map (Over.homMk Z.hom).op (F.presheafHomObjHomEquiv (ψ.hom i)) =
      D₁.hom (Z.hom ≫ f i) Z.hom (b ≫ p' j) ≫
        pullHom ((F.map (p' j).op.toLoc).toFunctor.map (ψ.hom (α j))) b _ _ ≫
        D₂.hom (Z.hom ≫ f i) (b ≫ p' j) Z.hom := by
    have := ψ.comm _ Z.hom (b ≫ p' j) rfl (by grind)
    dsimp [presheafHomObjHomEquiv, pullHom] at this ⊢
    simp [mapComp'_inv_naturality, Cat.Hom.comp_toFunctor,
      Functor.comp_obj, Cat.Hom.hom_inv_id_toNatTrans_app_assoc, ← reassoc_of% this,
      D₂.hom_self _ _ rfl, F.mapComp'_id_comp_inv_app, ← Functor.map_comp,
      F.mapComp'_id_comp_hom_app_assoc]
  replace hφ := congr_fun (congr_arg DescentData.Hom.hom hφ) j
  dsimp at hφ
  simp only [this, hφ]

include w H₃ H₄ in
/-- **Descent of morphisms between two descent data, from local hypotheses at their
components.** If the descent of morphisms between the components of `D₁` and `D₂` holds along
the pullback of the sieve generated by `f'` to each `X i`, and is separated along its pullback
to each chosen fibre product `X i₁ ×_S X i₂`, then restriction along the refinement is a
bijection from the morphisms `D₁ ⟶ D₂` to the morphisms between their restrictions.

This is the form in which Stacks 02ZD is used when the sheaf condition is available only for
*some* objects of the fibres — for instance the fpqc sheaf condition for the presheaf of
morphisms, which holds for quasi-coherent modules and not for arbitrary ones. -/
lemma bijective_pullFunctor_map :
    Function.Bijective ((pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p')
      (w_comp_id w)).map : (D₁ ⟶ D₂) → _) :=
  ⟨injective_pullFunctor_map w H₃, surjective_pullFunctor_map w H₃ sq H₄⟩

end Pair

include w in
/-- **Full faithfulness of the refinement functor from local hypotheses at the components.**
If for every pair `D₁, D₂` of descent data the descent of morphisms between their components
holds along the pullback of the sieve generated by `f'` to each `X i`, and is separated along
its pullback to each chosen fibre product `X i₁ ×_S X i₂`, then the refinement functor
`F.DescentData f ⥤ F.DescentData f'` is fully faithful.

The hypotheses are taken at the components of the two descent data, which is all the proof
uses; the form asking for the sheaf condition at *arbitrary* objects `M N` of the fibres, as
Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData.fullyFaithfulPullFunctor` does through
`CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsPrestack`, is strictly stronger. -/
lemma nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor
    (H₃ : ∀ (D₁ D₂ : F.DescentData f) (i : ι),
      Presieve.IsSheafFor (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i) (D₂.obj i))
        (refSieve f' (𝟙 (X i)) (f i)).arrows)
    (sq : ∀ i₁ i₂, ChosenPullback (f i₁) (f i₂))
    (H₄ : ∀ (D₁ D₂ : F.DescentData f) (i₁ i₂ : ι),
      Presieve.IsSeparatedFor (F.presheafHom (D₁.obj i₁) (D₂.obj i₁))
        (refSieve f' (sq i₁ i₂).p₁ (sq i₁ i₂).p).arrows) :
    Nonempty (pullFunctor F (f := f) (p := 𝟙 _) (f' := f') (p' := p')
      (w_comp_id w)).FullyFaithful :=
  (Functor.FullyFaithful.nonempty_iff_map_bijective _).2 fun D₁ D₂ ↦
    bijective_pullFunctor_map w (H₃ D₁ D₂) sq (H₄ D₁ D₂)

end Refinement

end Pseudofunctor.DescentData

namespace Pseudofunctor

variable {F : Pseudofunctor (LocallyDiscrete Cᵒᵖ) Cat.{v', u'}}

/-- If the descent of morphisms relative to a family `g : Y k ⟶ W` is separated, i.e. the
functor from the fibre over `W` to the descent data relative to `g` is faithful, then for any
`a : W ⟶ T` the presheaf of morphisms between two objects over `T` is separated for the sieve
on `Over.mk a` generated by `g`. -/
lemma isSeparatedFor_presheafHom_of_faithful {W : C} {κ : Type t} {Y : κ → C} (g : ∀ k, Y k ⟶ W)
    [(F.toDescentData g).Faithful] {T : C} (a : W ⟶ T) (M N : F.obj (.mk (op T))) :
    Presieve.IsSeparatedFor (F.presheafHom M N)
      ((Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk a)).symm (Sieve.ofArrows Y g)).arrows := by
  intro x t₁ t₂ h₁ h₂
  refine (F.toDescentData g).map_injective (DescentData.hom_ext (fun k ↦ ?_))
  have hk : ((Sieve.overEquiv (Over.mk a)).symm (Sieve.ofArrows Y g)).arrows
      (Over.homMk (g k) : Over.mk (g k ≫ a) ⟶ Over.mk a) := ⟨_, 𝟙 _, g k, ⟨k⟩, by simp⟩
  have key := (h₁ _ hk).trans (h₂ _ hk).symm
  dsimp [presheafHom] at key
  dsimp [toDescentData]
  rw [LocallyDiscreteOpToCat.map_eq_pullHom t₁ (g k) (g k ≫ a) (g k ≫ a) rfl rfl,
    LocallyDiscreteOpToCat.map_eq_pullHom t₂ (g k) (g k ≫ a) (g k ≫ a) rfl rfl, key]

end Pseudofunctor

namespace PreZeroHypercover

/-- The sieve generated by the base change of a family of morphisms with fixed target
`𝒱 = {V j ⟶ U}` along `q : W ⟶ U` is the pullback along `q` of the sieve generated by `𝒱`. -/
lemma ofArrows_pullback₁ {U : C} (𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{w} U) {W : C} (q : W ⟶ U)
    [∀ j, HasPullback q (𝒱.f j)] :
    Sieve.ofArrows (𝒱.pullback₁ q).X (𝒱.pullback₁ q).f =
      Sieve.pullback q (Sieve.ofArrows 𝒱.X 𝒱.f) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · rintro Y a ⟨T, c, _, ⟨j⟩, fac⟩
    dsimp at fac
    refine ⟨_, c ≫ pullback.snd q (𝒱.f j), _, ⟨j⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [← fac, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, pullback.condition]
  · rintro Y a ⟨T, c, _, ⟨j⟩, fac⟩
    exact ⟨_, pullback.lift a c fac.symm, _, ⟨j⟩, by simp⟩

end PreZeroHypercover

namespace Limits.ChosenPullback

/-- The chosen pullback given by `Limits.pullback` when the pullback exists. -/
@[sga "3 V 1.2"]
noncomputable def ofHasPullback {X₁ X₂ S : C} (f₁ : X₁ ⟶ S) (f₂ : X₂ ⟶ S) [HasPullback f₁ f₂] :
    ChosenPullback f₁ f₂ where
  pullback := Limits.pullback f₁ f₂
  p₁ := pullback.fst f₁ f₂
  p₂ := pullback.snd f₁ f₂
  condition := pullback.condition
  isLimit := (IsPullback.of_hasPullback f₁ f₂).isLimit

/-- The first projection of `ofHasPullback f₁ f₂` is `pullback.fst f₁ f₂`. -/
@[simp]
lemma ofHasPullback_p₁ {X₁ X₂ S : C} (f₁ : X₁ ⟶ S) (f₂ : X₂ ⟶ S) [HasPullback f₁ f₂] :
    (ofHasPullback f₁ f₂).p₁ = pullback.fst f₁ f₂ := rfl

/-- The structure morphism to `S` of `ofHasPullback f₁ f₂` is `pullback.fst f₁ f₂ ≫ f₁`. -/
@[simp]
lemma ofHasPullback_p {X₁ X₂ S : C} (f₁ : X₁ ⟶ S) (f₂ : X₂ ⟶ S) [HasPullback f₁ f₂] :
    (ofHasPullback f₁ f₂).p = pullback.fst f₁ f₂ ≫ f₁ := rfl

end Limits.ChosenPullback

namespace Functor

open IsFibered

variable {𝒳 : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} 𝒳]

/-- The functor `𝒮_U ⥤ DD(𝒰)` sending an object of the fibre of a fibred category `p : 𝒳 ⥤ C`
over `U` to its canonical descent datum relative to a family `𝒰 = {U i ⟶ U}` of morphisms with
fixed target. -/
noncomputable abbrev toFamilyDescentDatum (p : 𝒳 ⥤ C) [p.IsFibered] {U : C}
    (𝒰 : PreZeroHypercover.{w} U) : p.Fiber U ⥤ FamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰 :=
  (pullbackPseudofunctor p).toDescentData 𝒰.f

/-- **Stacks 0GEA.**
Let `𝒱 = {V j ⟶ U} ⟶ 𝒰 = {U i ⟶ U}` be a morphism of families of morphisms with fixed target
given by `𝟙 U`, a reindexing `α : J → I` and morphisms `V j ⟶ U (α j)`, and let `p` be a fibred
category. Assume that the fibre products `U i₁ ×_U U i₂`, `U i ×_U V j` and
`U i₁ ×_U U i₂ ×_U V j` exist, that `𝒮_U ⟶ DD(𝒱)` is an equivalence, that `𝒮_{U i} ⟶ DD(𝒱_i)`
is fully faithful for every `i`, and that `𝒮_{U i₁ ×_U U i₂} ⟶ DD(𝒱_{i₁i₂})` is faithful for
every `i₁, i₂`, where `𝒱_i` and `𝒱_{i₁i₂}` are the base changes of `𝒱`. Then `𝒮_U ⟶ DD(𝒰)` is
an equivalence. -/
@[stacks 0GEA]
theorem isEquivalence_toFamilyDescentDatum_of_homOver {p : 𝒳 ⥤ C} [p.IsFibered] {U : C}
    {𝒰 : PreZeroHypercover.{w} U} {𝒱 : PreZeroHypercover.{w'} U} (Φ : 𝒱.HomOver 𝒰 (𝟙 U))
    [∀ i₁ i₂, HasPullback (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂)]
    [∀ i j, HasPullback (𝒰.f i) (𝒱.f j)]
    [∀ i₁ i₂ j, HasPullback (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁) (𝒱.f j)]
    (h₂ : (toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒱).IsEquivalence)
    (h₃ : ∀ i, Nonempty (toFamilyDescentDatum p (𝒱.pullback₁ (𝒰.f i))).FullyFaithful)
    (h₄ : ∀ i₁ i₂, (toFamilyDescentDatum p
      (𝒱.pullback₁ (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁))).Faithful) :
    (toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰).IsEquivalence := by
  have w : ∀ j, Φ.h₀ j ≫ 𝒰.f (Φ.s₀ j) = 𝒱.f j :=
    fun j ↦ (Φ.w₀ j).trans (Category.comp_id _)
  have H₃ : ∀ (i : 𝒰.I₀) (M N : (pullbackPseudofunctor p).obj (.mk (op (𝒰.X i)))),
      Presieve.IsSheafFor ((pullbackPseudofunctor p).presheafHom M N)
        (DescentData.refSieve 𝒱.f (𝟙 (𝒰.X i)) (𝒰.f i)).arrows := by
    intro i M N
    have hpre : (pullbackPseudofunctor p).IsPrestackFor
        (Sieve.pullback (𝒰.f i) (Sieve.ofArrows 𝒱.X 𝒱.f)).arrows := by
      rw [← 𝒱.ofArrows_pullback₁ (𝒰.f i), Sieve.ofArrows, IsPrestackFor_generate_iff,
        isPrestackFor_ofArrows_iff]
      exact h₃ i
    exact ((pullbackPseudofunctor p).isPrestackFor_iff_isSheafFor' _).1 hpre M N (𝟙 _)
  have H₄ : ∀ (i₁ i₂ : 𝒰.I₀)
      (M N : (pullbackPseudofunctor p).obj (.mk (op (𝒰.X i₁)))),
      Presieve.IsSeparatedFor ((pullbackPseudofunctor p).presheafHom M N)
        (DescentData.refSieve 𝒱.f (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂))
          (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁)).arrows := by
    intro i₁ i₂ M N
    have := h₄ i₁ i₂
    have h := isSeparatedFor_presheafHom_of_faithful (F := pullbackPseudofunctor p)
      (𝒱.pullback₁ (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂) ≫ 𝒰.f i₁)).f
      (pullback.fst (𝒰.f i₁) (𝒰.f i₂)) M N
    rwa [𝒱.ofArrows_pullback₁] at h
  obtain ⟨hff⟩ := DescentData.nonempty_fullyFaithful_pullFunctor
    (F := pullbackPseudofunctor p) (f := 𝒰.f) (f' := 𝒱.f) (α := Φ.s₀) (p' := Φ.h₀) w
    (fun _ _ i ↦ H₃ i _ _) (fun i₁ i₂ ↦ .ofHasPullback _ _) (fun _ _ i₁ i₂ ↦ H₄ i₁ i₂ _ _)
  have hff' : (FamilyDescentDatum.pullFunctor p Φ).FullyFaithful := hff
  have := hff'.full
  have := hff'.faithful
  have := h₂
  have e : toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰 ⋙ FamilyDescentDatum.pullFunctor p Φ ≅
      toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒱 :=
    DescentData.toDescentDataCompPullFunctorIso _ _ ≪≫
      Functor.isoWhiskerRight (Cat.Hom.toNatIso ((pullbackPseudofunctor p).mapId _)) _ ≪≫
      Functor.leftUnitor _
  have := Functor.Faithful.of_comp_iso e
  have := Functor.Full.of_comp_faithful_iso e
  have : (toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰 ⋙ FamilyDescentDatum.pullFunctor p Φ).IsEquivalence :=
    Functor.isEquivalence_of_iso e.symm
  have := Functor.essSurj_of_comp_fully_faithful (toFamilyDescentDatum p 𝒰)
    (FamilyDescentDatum.pullFunctor p Φ)
  exact { }

end Functor

end CategoryTheory

